; setline_integer_sample_at_k: k is a count, so k itself is out of domain.
;
; The top of a k = 3 domain is 2. Writing 3 is the off-by-one a check
; written as `v <= k` lets through, and it is easy to write that way because
; k is the number on the stack and k-1 is not. integer_alloc writes 2 into
; the same sample and succeeds, so the pair brackets the bound from both
; sides.

PUSH 4
PUSH 3
XSMX r0          ; integer sample, k = 3, domain {0, 1, 2}

PUSH 1
PUSH 3           ; k, one past the top value k-1
SETLINE r0
HALT
